==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|un|roll}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-unroll.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[straighten]] something that has been [[roll]]ed, [[twist]]ed or [[curl]]ed.
#: '' '''Unroll''' your sleeping bag and spread it on the floor of the tent.''
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[emerge]], be [[reveal]]ed or become [[apparent]]; to [[unfold]].
#: ''We will have to see how the events '''unroll'''.''
# {{lb|en|transitive|programming|compilation}} To replace (a [[loop]] in a [[program]]) with a [[repetitive]] [[sequence]] of the individual [[instruction]]s that the loop would carry out, sometimes used as an [[optimization]].
#: {{syn|en|unwind}}

